  "modeling_notes": [
    "The Theory and Application curriculum is the canonical broad-computing B.S. path. Cybersecurity and Information Technology are complete alternate curriculum variants, not elective concentrations inside the canonical track.",
    "The catalog's categorical requirements close exactly to 136 credits for Theory and Application and Information Technology and 137 credits for Cybersecurity. Semester-by-semester synopsis tables were used only to corroborate category arithmetic and were not imported as additional requirements.",
    "The 34-credit VMI Core allocation includes the required writing, speaking, history, mathematics, science, leadership, and human-performance credits. ROTC is a separate 12-credit allocation. Civilizations and Cultures, writing-intensive, and capstone rules are retained as overlays because they are satisfied within those allocations.",
    "Cybersecurity's statistics requirement is conditional on the chosen Core mathematics sequence. The catalog offsets the extra three statistics credits with a 21-versus-24-credit free-elective range, keeping the track total at 137."
  ],
